{
  "chapter": "evals/online-evals",
  "tier": "drill",
  "notes": [
    "Online scoring is stratified sampling. A fixed share of everything, taken",
    "systematically by position rather than randomly so the plan is reproducible, plus",
    "every run matching a stratum where failures live.",
    "A run matching two strata is still scored once. The rate per stratum is what the plan",
    "actually achieved, in basis points, rounded with floor(x + 0.5). An empty stratum",
    "reports 0 — there was nothing to sample.",
    "The second half is the boundary shadow cannot cross. A shadowed agent runs with writes",
    "disabled, so a shadow run that wanted to write proves nothing about the write path.",
    "Only canary and production validate it, which is what makes canary non-optional for an",
    "agent that moves money, however clean the shadow results look."
  ],
  "policy": {
    "baselineEveryNth": 5,
    "always": ["escalated", "retried", "costOutlier"]
  },
